{
  "slug": "smoked-cod-potato-breakfast-hash",
  "name": "Seared cod and potato hash",
  "description": "Fresh cod fillet seared hard for a smoky edge, then flaked through a crisp potato, onion and bell pepper hash. No smoked fish needed — the colour comes from the pan.",
  "iconKey": "bowl_dash",
  "instructions": [
    "Dice the potato small and cook it in a wide skillet with the olive oil over medium-high heat until crisp and tender, about 12 minutes.",
    "Add the onion and bell pepper and cook until they soften and colour at the edges, about 4 minutes.",
    "Season the cod fillet with the salt and the black pepper, lay it on the hash and cover the pan for 4 minutes, until the fish is opaque.",
    "Flake the cod into large pieces, fold it gently through the hash and divide between two bowls."
